# Git & GitHub Complete Notes for Developers

## What is Version Control?

Version Control System (VCS) is used to track and manage source code changes over time.

### Problems Solved

* Multiple developers working on same project
* Code history tracking
* Rollback to previous versions
* Team collaboration
* Code auditing (who changed what and when)

### Popular Version Control Systems

* Git
* GitHub
* BitBucket
* SVN (Legacy)

---

# Git vs GitHub

## Git

* Distributed Version Control System
* Installed on local machine
* Tracks code changes

## GitHub

* Cloud platform for hosting Git repositories
* Provides collaboration and repository management

### Interview Answer

Git is a version control system used to track code changes, whereas GitHub is a cloud-based platform used to host Git repositories and collaborate with teams.

---

# Git Architecture

```text
Working Tree
     ↓
Staging Area
     ↓
Local Repository
     ↓
Remote Repository (GitHub)
```

### Working Tree

Developer writes code here.

### Staging Area

Files ready for commit.

### Local Repository

Stores commits locally.

### Remote Repository

Stores code in GitHub.

